CHỦ ĐỀ 8 — BAISHIYA — 22:20
5 TIÊU ĐỀ TIẾNG ANH VÀ 5 PROMPT THUMBNAIL TƯƠNG ỨNG

Đề xuất dùng phương án 1. Tạo ảnh 16:9, sau đó chèn chữ bằng phần mềm edit để tránh lỗi chữ. Không có trẻ em ở bất cứ vị trí nào trong ảnh.

1.
TITLE EN: How Denisovans Survived the Tibetan Plateau
TIẾNG VIỆT: Người Denisovan đã sống sót trên cao nguyên Tây Tạng như thế nào?
TEXT OVERLAY: HOW DID THEY LIVE?
PROMPT: Create a cinematic science-documentary YouTube thumbnail, 1280x720, 16:9. A dramatic empty limestone cave mouth on the northeastern Tibetan Plateau fills the right half; a single clean broken animal long-bone teaching replica sits large in the lower-left foreground. Show the high, dry, grassy Ganjia Basin beyond the cave, atmospheric mountain depth, no Everest-like snowy pyramid. Warm side light on the bone against a cool dark cave, realistic stone and bone textures, strong separation, only two main focal elements, clear mobile-size silhouette. Leave dark clean space in the upper-left for the editor to add the words HOW DID THEY LIVE? No people, no children anywhere, no skull faces, no fire, no glowing DNA, no logos, no watermark, no generated lettering. The bone is a generic educational replica, not a claim to show the actual Xiahe fossil. Intriguing and credible, with no gore.

2.
TITLE EN: A Tiny Rib Changed the Story of Ancient Tibet
TIẾNG VIỆT: Một mảnh xương sườn nhỏ đã thay đổi câu chuyện về Tây Tạng cổ đại
TEXT OVERLAY: TINY BONE. BIG CLUE.
PROMPT: Create a photorealistic 16:9 documentary thumbnail at 1280x720. Hero macro view of one small curved rib-like teaching fragment resting on neutral archival foam, sharp natural pores and a gentle fracture edge. A faint, defocused limestone cave entrance appears in the distant upper-right background. Cool conservation-lab lighting with a warm rim on the small fragment; the fragment occupies roughly one-third of the frame and remains readable on a phone. Leave clean dark space in the upper-left for editor-added text TINY BONE. BIG CLUE. No humans or hands, no children anywhere, no full skeleton, no jawbone, no blood, no fabricated excavation labels or dates, no glowing effects, no logos, no watermark, no generated text. Treat the fragment as an educational stand-in, not an authenticated photograph of Xiahe 2.

3.
TITLE EN: The Survival Story Hidden in Broken Bones
